          "distinct": true,
          "id": "b11e9a69fd672e61fd43c2984f5f5898fa45f9b8",
          "message": "test(velvet): answer the mutation survivors in the async helpers, the effect order and the drag overlay (#1479)\n\n## What & why\n\nMutation survivors on main are answered here, with tests wherever the code is reachable.\n\n- **`ApplicationVisibility`:**\n  - The window-visibility decisions move out of the Windows and macOS `#if` arms into platform-neutral members (`IsHiddenFrom`, `IsMinimized`, `KeepLooking` and helpers), now unit-tested on every platform.\n  - Only the raw interop statements stay inside the arms: `EnumThreadWindows`, `SendForObject` and the selector registrations. They are declared unreachable, because the editor CI runs in defines neither `UNITY_EDITOR_WIN` nor `UNITY_EDITOR_OSX`.\n  - The macOS per-window check now reads both window flags for every window instead of short-circuiting. Both are side-effect-free reads, and the result is the same.\n- **`RetryPolicy`:** cases for the main-thread reads of the online and focus signals, and for a cancellation that arrives as the connection returns. `By`'s compute-first read is declared equivalent.\n- **`ComponentRegistry`:** an effect-order case with keyed containers of two components each, reordered.\n- **`DragOverlayHost`:** a root-fiber mount case. The version bump's sign is declared equivalent.\n\nTwo mutants remain unmeasured because they time out by looping forever: `DragOverlayHost.cs:97` and `ComponentBoundarySearch.cs:81`. A test cannot answer them.\n\nNo behaviour change for users; no doc or changelog impact.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) — Unity suites run in CI\n- [x] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it — kills are decided by the next mutation record run\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches (guides, READMEs, CLAUDE.md) — or this PR has no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-` — inline under `## [Unreleased]` on a maintenance line with no `scripts/release/compile_changelog.py` (pure refactors are omitted by convention)\n- [x] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
