          "distinct": true,
          "id": "5bf7b905acd275c288708718b56b9bf79f7dc711",
          "message": "perf(velvet): place appended rows from the last one and leave a discarded row's bindings registered (#1507)\n\nNo issue: performance work on the js-framework-benchmark Create, Replace and Clear operations.\n\n## What & why\n\nA per-stage profile of Replace and Clear on main (temporary instrumentation, on a scratch branch and not in this change) found:\n\n- **`AddPhase` and the other insert loops resolved each child's physical index from slot zero.** `LogicalChildSlots.ToPhysical` pays one invisible-child check per child it passes, and a row with three children paid it 0, 1 and 2 times: 3000 calls over 1000 rows. The loops that add rows at ascending slots now insert through `LogicalSlotCursor.Insert`, which walks on from the slot it last inserted at. Covers the indexed `AddPhase`, the keyed `Pass1TailAdd`, the synchronous keyed tail add and pure insert, and the desync rebuild.\n- **`FiberNodePatcher.AddClass` and `RemoveClass` ran the full ownership ladder for every class.** They now take the plain-class shortcut `ApplyClassNames` has, through one shared predicate (non-empty, and none of `:`, `[`, `(`, `_`, `!`). Every check in the ladder needs one of those marks to succeed.\n- **Teardown unregistered the event bindings of every element below a discarded row.** They now stay registered, as the click gates and text-item callbacks already do; the one unbind action with state of its own, a Button's click-event slot, is dropped by `ForgetDiscarded`.\n- **Teardown took the shown-image watch off every element.** It is released only for an element whose layer map records a watch, ahead of `ClearAll`, which drops that map.\n\n## Measured\n\nSame-CPU medians are in a comment on this pull request once the runs finish.\n\n## Examined and left alone\n\n- `ClearElementSideTables` (33 tables per element), the weak-table removals and `RemoveCleaned`: each is a small share of teardown and none has a removal that is provably free.\n- `ProcessKeyedNode` and `PatchOrReplaceAtSlot` still resolve a matched row from slot zero; Replace, which matches nothing, does not reach them.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Tests pass locally (EditMode / PlayMode / generator tests as applicable) -- no Unity here; the suites run in CI\n- [ ] New regression tests were verified red without the change and green with it -- not run locally; `Test ▸ base-red` runs the cases the base is expected to fail\n- [x] Docs are updated for every fact this change touches -- no guide describes these paths, no doc impact\n- [x] CHANGELOG fragment added for behavior/perf changes, named for the branch with `/` as `-`\n- [ ] Known gaps or deliberate deferrals discovered here are filed as issues with acceptance criteria -- none filed\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01FoK7YxdRjMGmfmRkEEmS88)_",
