          "distinct": false,
          "id": "046532408a00a5ae664eb7e6bb8e5c479b44a2c3",
          "message": "fix(velvet): resolve a container's old instances once, before the walk writes to it (#1556)\n\nRefs #1545\n\nFirst refactor of the render/commit split that fixes #1545.\n\nThe diff found each old instance by reading the live child list at its logical slot (`parent.ElementAt(LogicalChildSlots.ToPhysical(...))`) — in `PatchOrReplaceAtSlot`, the suffix trim, `ProcessKeyedNode` and `CommitLeaf` — so the tree it was writing doubled as the old tree. A container's old instances are now resolved once when the walk enters it, into a pooled `OldSlotOccupants` (slot occupant and wrapper-resolved element), and the diff reads only that; each entry is read once, guarded by the used-key and used-index sets. A parked indexed or keyed pass keeps its array, so a resume no longer re-reads `slotStart + i`.\n\nThe live tree can still change under an open walk, and the array follows:\n- A nested `FiberCommitWork.DrainPendingWork` that finishes a parked inline pass mid-walk writes rows into the same container; open general walks re-resolve after it (`ReconcilerContext.OpenOldInstances`).\n- `FiberZLayerCoordinator`'s slot swaps between slices (a `hover:z-10` restack, `Restack`, `Reorder`) replace the old element with the new one in the rented arrays (`NoteSlotOccupantChanged` → `ReplaceOccupant`) and in the rows a parked keyed Pass 2 already took (`ReplaceParkedRow`).\n- A Portal drain that mounts over a parked parent sets the parked state aside instead of moving it out, so the parent stays registered as parked; its `Arrange` converts nothing until the parked diff finishes, where main could convert between slices.\n\nUser-visible: a time-sliced update of a keyed list no longer leaves an extra, empty child when an `absolute hover:z-*` row stops being hovered while the update is paused after reaching it (`### Fixed`). `Reconciler.Dispose` now also discards a parked indexed pass.\n\nTests: `ContainerOldInstanceReadTests` (EditMode) refuses any slot read — `ElementAt`, `ToPhysical` or a `TryGetPhysical` index used as an indexer — in the diff loops outside the portal row scans; `OldSlotOccupantsPoolingTests` pins every rent's return and the reset; `FlatListReconcileAllocationTests` pins zero allocation re-reconciling an unchanged list; four `ZIndexStackingTests` cases restack a row between slices; `TimeSlicedPortalDrainParkTests` pins the parked registration through a Portal drain.\n\nNext in the stack: one seam for the walk's host writes, then the patch split.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
