          "distinct": true,
          "id": "66275d963a2a79fa847fa7d8d66141edd4d74c78",
          "message": "fix(velvet): read a parked list's unreached row's Providers from the committed baseline (#1603)\n\nCloses #1589\n\nA row of a keyed list whose Transition render parked, and which re-rendered on its own before the render reached it, read the wrong Provider. It got the parked, uncommitted value from the first row holding a component at the same position. For example, `TimeSlicedFiberTests` read `g1-0` where React reads the committed `g0-7`.\n\nThe cause is in `FiberContextSpine`. Its keyed edge walked the parent's `ReconcilingTree ?? PreviousTree`. While the pass is parked, `PreviousTree` holds the parked render's output, but the row's `SourceTree` is the committed baseline. The node comparison therefore failed, the walk fell back to the key alone, and it stopped at the first container with that position.\n\nThe edge now reads `OwnOutput(ancestor, child)`. That is the parent's `PendingOldTree` (the committed baseline the parked pass started from) when `child.SourceTree` is that tree, and otherwise `ReconcilingTree ?? PreviousTree` as before. A row the parked pass already reached keeps reading the parked output, which is what it rendered.\n\nThe detached half of the issue thread (VirtualList items and Portal children reading Context captured at setup) stays open as #1590. It is not touched here.\n\nTests in `TimeSlicedFiberTests`:\n- The case pinning the wrong reading now expects the row's committed value; it is red on the base.\n- A characterization pins that a row the parked pass reached reads the parked output.\n\nCHANGELOG under `unreleased/`. No `Documentation~` change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-12T12:38:33+09:00",
          "tree_id": "f19bd7b8581ae3169539480e91fe0ba1cacb5da4",
