          "distinct": true,
          "id": "6d7e97a96c675987281f5f8f5df7ac92f58122f5",
          "message": "perf(velvet): find an inline fiber's slot limit from its own sibling, not the head of the chain (#1711)\n\nRefs #1696. This is step 7 of the plan: the walk on the fiber side that a row's own update repeats in proportion to its siblings.\n\n`FiberCommitWork.NextInlineSiblingSlotStart` finds where an inline fiber's rows end. It used to walk every sibling fiber from the head of the list. A placed fiber (`MountSlotCount >= 0`) now starts from its own `Sibling` and returns the first placed later start on the same mount point. An unplaced fiber still reads from the head.\n\n## Why that is safe\n\nThe sibling chain is ordered by `MountSlotStart` wherever `MountSlotCount >= 0` on one mount point. The code does not prove that order.\n\n- **Measured.** The function was instrumented to log any out-of-order pair, and any case where the first later sibling differed from the minimum. Across about 6,700 keyed, reorder, portal, boundary, Suspense, fallback, inline-slot and EventLog cases, neither was logged.\n- **Pinned.** `InlineSlotChainOrderTests` holds the order across the changes it tests. Making `ComponentFiber.CommitChildOrder` a no-op turns 4 of its 5 order rows red.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Red on the base.** One case, `Given_ASiblingStartingBetweenTheNextStartAndTheFiber_…`, is red there: the base returns 5 where 9 is right. The other cases are declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`, each with a perturbation:\n- Starting an unplaced fiber from `Sibling` turns its case red.\n- Adding one allocation per `Claim` turns `ContextSpineRowUpdateAllocationTests` red.\n\n**`FiberContextSpine.Push`.** Its reported growth from 24 to 33 blocks is a one-iteration artifact: the claim table grows once per process. In steady state the count is 14 blocks at both 250 and 2,000 rows. The new allocation case holds that.\n\n**Benchmark.** `RenderPathScalingBenchmarks`, PlayMode `-velvetBenchmarkFull`, base and branch back to back, median ms per update. Blocks are 14 in both arms.\n\n| Rows | Base | Branch |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| 250 | 0.42 | 0.26 |\n| 2,000 | ~3.5 | ~1.8 |\n\n**Targeted runs.** 1,372 cases ran across the inline-slot, boundary, Suspense, fallback, portal, context, EventLog and slot fixtures. All passed, and none was inconclusive. `compile_check.py` and the cheap guards pass.\n\nNo CHANGELOG fragment, since the change is internal.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
