          "distinct": true,
          "id": "ec52c6786b152b9551f31eb397068871290722da",
          "message": "fix(velvet): detach a replaced ref in its host's place and run imperative handles in hook order (#1712)\n\nCloses #1674. Two of its three commit-order differences from React are fixed here. The third moves to v4.0.0 as #1710, because fixing it needs an API change.\n\n## What changed\n\n**A: replaced ref callbacks detach in their host's place.** `CommitLayoutBatch` now takes the ref queue before the cleanup pass. `RunCleanupPass` places each detach the same way `FiberRefPlacement.Interleave` places attaches, so a replaced ref detaches where React's mutation walk reaches its host. Before, every replaced ref detached at the head of the commit, ahead of every cleanup. `DetachReplacedRefs` is gone, replaced by `DetachReplacedRef(element)`.\n\n**B: imperative handles attach in hook order among the layout effects.** React's `useImperativeHandle` is a layout effect (`mountImperativeHandle`). `HookImperativeHandleSlot.LayoutEffectsBefore` records how many layout effects come before the handle, and `HookEffectExecutor.RunFactories` runs the handle between them. Before, `RunLayoutSetup` ran every handle ahead of the fiber's layout setups.\n\n**C: calling a ref callback with `null` when it returned no cleanup** is not done here. `refCallback:` is `Func<VisualElement, Action>`, which declares a non-null element. Existing callers written as `el => { …; return null; }` would throw at detach, and an attempt turned 10 existing cases red. `react-migration.md` now states the deviation: a callback that returns no cleanup is not called on detach, so return a cleanup to observe it. #1710 tracks the 4.0 change.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `HandleAndRefDetachEventLogTests` holds the logs from #1674. Each A and B case is red on `main` and green here:\n  - B, mount: `render:H lay:A handle:H lay:B`, where `main` logs `render:H handle:H lay:A lay:B`.\n  - B, update: the same order.\n  - A: the replaced ref's `ref-x:A` lands after the children's layout cleanups, not ahead of their insertion effects.\n\n  A handle declared before every layout effect is the control, and it passes on both.\n- 185 targeted cases pass. They cover the ref, handle and EventLog fixtures and the cases a review found red under C. A wider run of 389 cases also passed; it included `DrainExceptionRecoveryTests`.\n- `compile_check.py` passes.\n\nThe CHANGELOG fragment is under `### Fixed`, for A and B.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
