          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7e156844cf999cd7d770710aa7aec38020743dce",
          "message": "refactor(velvet): read portal, Suspense and structural-variant rows from the row model (#1713)\n\nRefs #1696. This is step 4 of the row model. The element readers named in the design now read the model through `Rows`, `RowAt` and `PhysicalRange`, instead of walking the live child list. No behaviour changes.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **New model reads.** `ContainerRows.RowAt` and `ContainerRows.PhysicalRange`, each with a `ChildListWrites` façade.\n- **Moved readers.**\n  - `ChildReconciler.HideMountUnderHiddenSuspense`.\n  - `GeneralPathReconciler.AddWithPortalChildren`, `HoldsAMotionInPortal` and `CollectPortalExits`. `SetPrimaryHidden` no longer rents a `RenderedChildrenCache`.\n  - `ReconcilerContext.SyncPortalRowFamilies`, with one `Rows` call per portal, and the `Anchor` ends.\n  - `FiberElementCleaner.CleanupPortal`'s range.\n  - `FiberNodePatcher.ApplyStructuralVariants`, which now makes one `Rows` call.\n- **Where moved readers index.** They now index the container's content element. The old code converted a slot on the content element, then indexed `target.hierarchy`. The two differ only for a target whose `contentContainer` is another element.\n- **`RenderedChildrenCache` stays.** `FiberRefPlacement` (`LogicalElementTree`) and `PreOrderTeardown` still read a snapshot from it while a pass runs.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Read count.** `StructuralVariantRowReadScalingTests` counts reads over one `ApplyStructuralVariants` call at 500 and 1,000 rows. With step 3's loop the reads grew 1.999×, and the test caps that growth at 1.5×; with this change it passes.\n- **New model reads.** `ContainerRowsTests` adds `RowAt` and `PhysicalRange` cases at sizes 12 and 700. Cutting `RowAt` reddens only its two cases, and cutting `PhysicalRange` reddens only its two.\n- **Targeted runs.** All green, none inconclusive:\n\n  | Fixtures | Passed |\n  |---|---:|\n  | EventLog, structural, z-index, slot addressing and `ContainerRowsTests` | 221 |\n  | Portal | 245 |\n  | Suspense, presence and motion hold | 414 |\n  | Routing and documentation guards | 82 |\n- **Guards.** `compile_check.py` and the cheap guards pass, and the refusal baseline is unchanged.\n\nThere is no CHANGELOG fragment, because the change is internal.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
