          "id": "5317eb044d0f3bbc105ea735d3a1c7332099c6f2",
          "message": "test(velvet): answer the 3.0.1 gate's sampled survivors in the row model (#1723)\n\nNo issue: these are the answers to the 3.0.1 release gate's sampled mutation survivors in the row model.\n\nOn main at 7e156844c, the release gate refuses 97 of the 400 mutants it samples: each survived and nobody answered for it. This PR answers the 44 in `ChildListWrites.cs`, `ContainerRows.cs`, `LogicalChildSlots.cs`, `HostCommitQueue.cs` and `ReconcilerBufferPool.cs`. The other two groups follow in their own PRs.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **31 new cases kill 32 of the survivors.**\n  - 24 are in `ContainerRowsTests`, 5 in `ContainerRowsPanelTests`, 1 in `LogicalChildSlotTests` and 1 in a new `PostOrderBuffersTests`.\n  - They cover the forwarding-container chain, a former container's removal and verification, the detach-time row counts, block splitting and collapsing, vacated slots, out-of-range reads, and buffer clearing.\n  - `RowModelAccess` (test-side) gains reflection readers for the block layout.\n  - Each case passes on main by design and carries a `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)` declaration.\n- **12 `MUTANT_SURVIVES` declarations answer the rest.** These are the only Runtime edits, and they are comments.\n  - 10 are `equivalent`: the mutated probe repeats a comparison made just before it, the write stores a value already held, or the loop always returns before the mutated bound.\n  - 2 are `unreachable`:\n    - `ContainerRows.Rows`'s skip loop cannot reach `BlockCount` when `slotStart < end <= _rendered`.\n    - Its clamp matters only for a negative `slotStart`, which no caller passes.\n  - The `HostCommitQueue` one rests on UI Toolkit's `Hierarchy.Insert` removing a child from its old parent before placing it. The engine's decompile shows this.\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe kill for each case is traced from the code. The next mutation record run measures them; this PR's CI measures that every case passes on main. No behaviour changes, so there is no CHANGELOG fragment and no `Documentation~` change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
