          "id": "45574ab70e8a7b6140d95619a08626422bc92d87",
          "message": "test(velvet): answer the 3.0.1 gate's sampled survivors in Component, Hooks, Routing and Styling (#1724)\n\nNo issue: this answers the sampled mutation survivors the 3.0.1 release gate found in Component, Hooks, Routing and Styling.\n\nOn main at 7e156844c, the release gate refuses 97 of the 400 mutants it samples, because each one survived and nobody answered for it. This PR answers the 22 in `ComponentContextStack`, `ComponentFiber`, `HookEffectExecutor`, `Hooks`, `RouteBlockerSlot`, `BackdropFilterLayer`, `FaceBorderOverlay`, `OutlineHosting`, `RingOverlay`, `StyleEaseCurve` and `StyleFontResolver`. #1723 answers the row model's survivors, and a third PR answers the rest of the reconciler's.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **15 new cases.** Each asserts state that an unanswered survivor left unread:\n  - the context stack reuses an emptied stack;\n  - `ComponentFiber` clears its caught-error flags;\n  - `RouteBlockerSlot` releases its predicate, its registration and its state callback;\n  - backdrop layers, face-border overlays and clip proxies leave their host when their class drops;\n  - a ring's mode change re-kinds its row;\n  - a non-timing class does not get an ease curve;\n  - a foreign or named-family font resolves the right asset;\n  - strict mode runs the factory of an imperative handle twice when no layout effect sits beside it.\n\n  Each passes on main and carries a `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)` declaration.\n- **5 `MUTANT_SURVIVES(equivalent)` declarations.** These are the only other edits under Runtime besides the `Hooks.cs` change below, and they are comments.\n  - The default of `mountDoubleInvoke` is never read outside the editor-only strict-mode block.\n  - UI Toolkit's `Hierarchy.Insert` takes an already-parented child out of its old parent before placing it, which makes the removal before the inserts in `OutlineHosting` and `RingOverlay` redundant.\n  - `StyleFontResolver`'s residual flags are read only when an asset was found.\n- **`Hooks.cs` stops refreshing `LayoutEffectsBefore` on update.** The mount branch already records an imperative handle's place among its component's layout effects. A valid program calls hooks in the same order every render, so the update branches rewrote the same value. The refresh mattered only when layout effects and handles swap places between renders, which breaks the rules of hooks and has no defined result in React.\n\n## Evidence\n\nEach case's kill is traced from the code. The next mutation record run measures them, and this PR's CI checks that every case passes on main. The `Hooks.cs` change leaves every valid program's order as it was: the in-order handle cases in `HandleAndRefDetachEventLogTests` still hold. No CHANGELOG fragment and no `Documentation~` change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
