          "distinct": true,
          "id": "b49143fafa70e0ed7077595a25d1340e8402407f",
          "message": "test(velvet): answer the 3.0.1 gate's sampled survivors in the row model, the layout commit, the error boundary and the z-layer coordinator (#1764)\n\nNo issue: answers to the 3.0.1 release gate.\n\nThe 3.0.1 release gate refuses nine sampled mutants that survived a record run with nothing answering for them, and holds one more unresolved. This answers all ten.\n\n## Cases\n\nEach new case reads state one of these survivors, or the unsampled one beside it, left unread:\n\n- **`ContainerRowsPanelTests`**: a hierarchy change announced inside a write for a child marks that child's parent for comparison (`ChildListWrites.NoteDuringOp` of the announced element's parent).\n- **`ZIndexStackingTests`**: a placeholder the z-layer arrangement retires and removes itself is released (`Release` in `DrainTeardownsUnder`).\n- **`PassBufferPoolReturnTests`**, two cases: the lists a layout commit takes and dedups its batch into go back to the pool. The deduped return in `TakeBatch` is sampled; the taken one beside it is not, and the same arrangement answers both.\n\nEach declares `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`.\n\n## Declarations\n\nSeven `MUTANT_SURVIVES` comments answer the rest. They are the only edits outside the test fixtures:\n\n- **`ContainerRows`**: the boundary in `Block.RemoveAt`, the uncleared `Anchors` in `Block.Empty`, `SkippedCount` (nothing reads it), and the boundary at the top of `ToLogical`.\n- **`FiberEffects`**: the standalone effect run, which only a fiber `Unmount` has left without a `Reconciler` reaches.\n- **`FiberErrorBoundary`**: the result after a boundary hands on its failed fallback, which returns to a boundary already disposed.\n- **`FiberPrimitiveElementPool`**: the Button's child-count test, the sibling of the Label's, already declared.\n\nNo behaviour changes, so there is no CHANGELOG fragment and no `Documentation~` change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-18T00:42:10+09:00",
