          "id": "cee633d971dcf1a842c17cfa452b3cf7932e52de",
          "message": "chore(velvet): release v3.0.1 (#1751)\n\nNo issue: the 3.0.1 release.\n\nCloses `## [Unreleased]` as `## [3.0.1] - 2026-11-17`: the seven fragments under `Changelog~/unreleased/` are\nfolded into the file, the version carries a fresh Highlights block, and `package.json` is at 3.0.1, the version\n`next_version.py` prints. `## [Unreleased — breaking]` was empty and stays standing over nothing, above the new\nsection. SECURITY.md's `3.0.x` row already marks the series 3.0.1 belongs to as supported, so the table is\nunchanged. No documentation impact beyond the CHANGELOG.\n\nTwo sentences of the folded font entries are corrected to what `FiberFontScope` does: a weight, italic or width\nclass keeps an inherited author font only where no `font-<name>` sits on its element or above it, since a\n`font-<name>` ancestor's family is the one it takes; and the per-update read of a parent's font is the mounted\ntree's, made at each update of the panel it is mounted on while it holds such an element.\n\nNo open pull request adds to `## [Unreleased — breaking]`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-18T12:14:30+09:00",
