          "distinct": true,
          "id": "a7ca6ce7a37e3346d8466a25707438c1c6428b3b",
          "message": "perf(velvet): skip the context spine walk over an output that holds nothing to push (#1717)\n\nCloses #1696. Closes #1509. Closes #1511.\n\nThis is the last step of the row model. A row updating its own state now costs the same at any list length. The branch contains #1715 and #1716. Until they merge, review only the commits after them.\n\n## What changed\n\n`FiberContextSpine.Push` walked every sibling VNode ahead of the row's own node, looking for context to push. With the slot reads already flat, that walk was the only part of the drain still growing with the list: 48 µs at 250 rows and 366 µs at 2,000.\n\n`FiberContextSpine.PushesNoContext` now skips the walk when the ancestor's output holds no Provider, Motion or memo node. With none of those, nothing can be pushed, whichever child is looked for. The answer is cached per output array on the ancestor's `ComponentFiber`, in `ContextFreeOutput` and `ContextFreeOutputAnswer`.\n\nThe skip is all or nothing. An output that holds any of those nodes still runs the full walk.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBenchmark: `RowSetState_Under*MemoizedRows` in `RenderPathScalingBenchmarks`, PlayMode with `-velvetBenchmarkFull`, median of 10.\n\n| Rows | Before (ms) | After (ms) | GC blocks, before and after |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| 250 | 0.129 | 0.051 | 14 |\n| 500 | 0.190 | 0.052 | 14 |\n| 1,000 | 0.324 | 0.053 | 14 |\n| 2,000 | 0.584 | 0.053 | 14 |\n\n`ContextSpineRowUpdateAllocationTests` gains two cases:\n- **The skip is taken.** The case reads the list fiber's cached answer after a row update. Deleting the skip leaves no answer, and the case turns red. It cannot compile on the base.\n- **A Provider is still pushed.** A row under a list inside a Provider still reads the provided value. The case is declared `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)`. Counting a Provider as pushing nothing turns it red.\n\n#1509 and #1511 no longer reproduce on this tree:\n- A keyed parent re-render with every row matched costs 14.1 µs per row at 500 rows and 11.8 µs at 2,000.\n- `HasMarkerClass` is called 0 times per matched update.\n- A swap of two rows makes N + 2 calls, one per row.\n\nTargeted EditMode runs:\n- The context, Suspense and Portal-context fixtures: 311 passed.\n- The guard fixtures: 128 passed.\n- `compile_check.py` passed. Neither the refusal baseline nor the duplication baseline changed.\n\n`RenderedChildrenCache` stays. `PreOrderTeardown` and `LogicalElementTree` rely on its snapshot, which deliberately does not see a change a callback makes to the children while it is held. A model read would see that change.\n\n#1571, the cost of placing portal children, is a separate PR.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
