          "distinct": true,
          "id": "94b74a354be201a11ba32b14e415aba545a5a859",
          "message": "fix(velvet): retime each class-timed transition by its own keyword, and read a variant swap's timing before the narrowing removes it (#1774)\n\nCloses #1569. Closes #1631.\n\n## #1569: each class-timed transition on its own keyword\n\nOn an element with a timing class, `StyleEaseCurve.OnRun` asked for the one keyword every transition resolved, and retimed nothing when the element's rules listed more than one (`transition-timing-function: ease-in, ease-out`). Those transitions kept UI Toolkit's curve. It now reads each transition's keyword from the curve the engine started it on, as the Motion tween path already did, and runs Tailwind's curve for it. `UssEasing.Is` holds the two-point test both paths use.\n\n## #1631: a variant swap's timing is read before the narrowing removes it\n\nDuring a variant swap, `MotionNativeTransitionGuard.Refresh` took the narrowers' longhands out of the swap's transition list before `LayoutIdLook.Narrow` and the opacity carry read it. A carry reads a list that does not name its property as no transition. So a layoutId Motion's rotate, corner radius, translate, scale or crossfaded opacity landed at once during a swap whose classes or stylesheet transition that property.\n\n- `MotionLayoutIdDriver.Compute` and `LayoutIdLook.StepTail` run `Narrow` before `Refresh`.\n- `Refresh` calls `MotionOpacity.Hold` before it removes anything, so the opacity carry's scheduled tail reads the list whichever of the two tails steps first.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `StyleEaseCurve` tests: under a two-keyword list, a transition runs on Tailwind's curve for its keyword rather than UI Toolkit's. Red on the base.\n- `MotionScheduledMechanicsTests`: a crossfade's own opacity, a mid-move rotate and a tail turn each run on the swap's timing. A fourth case holds the opacity tail back while the look tail steps and expects the swap's timing rather than 0.25. All four are red on the base.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
