          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8c91cee7fcd3a3ead95e9270485a6d60baa8db7f",
          "message": "perf(velvet): derive a text item's automatic minimum size per parent, and only where it can bind (#1788)\n\nCloses #1667.\n\nEach Label and Button carries `StyleFlexMinSizeManipulator`, which emulates a flex item's automatic minimum size (its min-content size) by writing an inline minimum. Every text item subscribed to its parent's `GeometryChangedEvent` and re-derived on each patch and each parent resize.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **One subscription per parent.** `StyleTextItemManipulator` keeps a `ParentHub` per parent (a `ConditionalWeakTable`, as `ColorReferenceWatch` does) with one static callback and its text leaves. A parent event re-derives a leaf only when the parent's direction moved, the leaf has not settled, or its minimum reads the parent's box (a percentage length, or a grid parent).\n- **Unchanged patches skip.** `Refresh` returns when the class array, the displayed text and the settled signature are unchanged.\n- **Measure only where the minimum can bind.** A wrapping, shrinkable row item whose width already holds its whole text carries no minimum, and its min-content is not measured; a signature term re-derives it once it is squeezed below that. A text whose widest run is its whole width is never released, since its minimum is that width. The room test runs after the signature, stand-down and undrawable-font guards.\n- `Velvet.FlexMinSize.Derive` is a `ProfilerMarker` around `Derive`, which the benchmark counts.\n- `styling-flexbox-and-gap.md` states which items carry a minimum.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `TextItemBaselinePanelTests`: the minimum each gated shape keeps (squeezed below its widest word, nowrap, shrink-0, column, percent max-width followed through a parent event, a direction flip, a text change, a one-word label settled again at its minimum) is declared green on the base with the perturbation that reddens it; a roomy row item carrying no minimum and the hub holding no leaf after a removal are red on the base.\n- `FlexMinSizeResizeBenchmarks` (PlayMode): 500 labels in a row and in a column, the container resized every frame; layout phases, GC and `Frame.Derive`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
