          "distinct": true,
          "id": "30321656e24f561e39551e8435ad4c07cfae47a6",
          "message": "refactor(velvet): record a removed row's removal and pool it after the pass's writes apply (#1727)\n\nRefs #1655. Refs #1545. Stacked on #1722.\n\nThis is step 1 of [the plan on #1655](https://github.com/s4k10503/velvet/issues/1655#issuecomment-6910564546). Removals become recorded list writes, and returning an element to its pool waits until those writes apply. Every slice still applies what it recorded, no later than where `FinishPass` starts, so what a user sees changes only in reads made mid-pass and in when a removed row's detach events fire.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Removals are recorded.** `ChildListWrites.RemoveRow` finds the row by reference and records its removal while a pass records. The model changes at once and the live list changes at apply. `HostCommitQueue.RemoveRow` routes it, and `FiberElementCleaner.RemoveCleaned` now calls that.\n  - A recorded removal no longer flushes the writes recorded before it.\n  - The take-down still runs in the walk: effects, refs, side tables, overlays.\n- **Pool returns wait.** While a pass is open, returning a removed element to its pool goes on `ReconcilerContext.PendingPoolReturns`. `FiberElementCleaner.ReleasePendingPoolReturns` drains it in `FinishPass`, after the recorded writes apply and before the retired z-layer reals are released.\n  - The order is kept: removed, then reset, then pooled.\n  - A throw while draining no longer skips the drains behind it.\n  - Dispose clears the queue.\n- **World-space Portal ranges** record their removal like any other row.\n\n## Behaviour\n\n- **Removed row.** A row removed in a pass stays in the live list until the pass's writes apply, and its pooled element is reset and returned only then.\n- **Pool reuse within one pass.** A later row in the same pass no longer rents the element just removed. A replacement in one pass therefore creates a new element where it used to reuse the old one. Pooling across passes is unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **`RecordedRemovalTests`.** Mid-pass, a later row reads that:\n  - the removed row is still in the live list;\n  - the model holds only the remaining row;\n  - the removed label is not yet reset;\n  - a rented label is a different instance.\n\n  After the reconcile, the removed label is the next one rented. A removal behind a replaced row no longer applies the replaced row's recorded insert early. Dispose leaves nothing queued.\n- **`RemovalDuringApplyTests`.** A removal made by a detach handler while the writes apply still waits for the drain.\n- **`OverlayRowRemovalTests`.** Ring and backdrop rows trimmed from a keyed list leave each remaining row followed by its own overlay.\n- **`HostCommitRoutingTests`.** The cleaner writes a row's removal only through the queue, and the pool drain runs after the apply.\n\nNo CHANGELOG fragment and no `Documentation~` change: no API changes, and the steps are internal.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- The cost of losing pool reuse within a pass is not measured yet. It needs the `benchmarks` run.\n- Teardown still runs in the walk. Its order (#1600), the passive cleanups (#1604) and the completion-only apply are later steps of #1655.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
