          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e0a05d4cbc637705dfc3072e5e5c6ca36eda8597",
          "message": "fix(velvet): plan a deletion's take-downs from the tree before its first cleanup runs (#1728)\n\nRefs #1655. Stacked on #1727.\n\nStep 2 of [the plan on #1655](https://github.com/s4k10503/velvet/issues/1655#issuecomment-6910564546), revised. The deletion walk now records which fibers and elements it takes down, and in what order, from the tree as it stood before the first cleanup. It then runs that plan. React walks a deletion by the fiber tree, so a cleanup that mutates host children cannot change what gets taken down. Before this change, Velvet read each element's children after earlier cleanups had run.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`PreOrderTeardown`** has a plan of `(fiber | element)` steps. Its `Take` either appends to the plan or takes the step down at once, depending on `PlansTakeDowns`. `RunPlan` executes the plan in order.\n- **`DeletionCommit`** plans its walk, then runs the plan in both `Run` and `TakeDownLeaving`. The placement reads (slot state, Portal ranges, z-layer placeholders, ref counts) already happened before the walk, and they stay there.\n- **`SuspenseOffscreenCommit`** keeps its inline walk. That walk deliberately reads whether a cleanup took the boundary's hold mid-walk.\n\n## Behaviour\n\nPreviously, when a deleted component's layout cleanup unlinked an element from its parent, the ref on that element stayed attached. The walk never reached the element. Now the ref detaches with the deletion, after the cleanup, which is React's order.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `DeletionCommitOrderEventLogTests` has a new case. A deleted component's layout cleanup unlinks its child's element, and the log reads `lay-x:M ref-x:Z`. On #1727 the log stops at `lay-x:M`.\n- The existing order cases still hold, including the two where a layout cleanup throws into a boundary.\n- `PreOrderTeardownAllocationTests` pins zero allocation on both the inline path and the plan path.\n\nNo `Documentation~` change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
