          "distinct": true,
          "id": "5b0297af148ab6c478ebff044d3d5b6e101c5d0c",
          "message": "perf(velvet): stop five Portal unmount, hide and reveal steps from searching per Portal (#1726)\n\nRefs #1718. Stacked on #1719.\n\nFive steps that unmount, hide or reveal Portals no longer search a list once per Portal or per fiber. Removing a Portal still shifts the ranges and fibers behind it by reading all of them, so unmounting many sibling Portals is not yet flat per Portal. The two remaining shifts are listed under Not covered.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`DefaultFamilyRoots.Release`** marks its root `Released` instead of searching `s_held`. The prune, which always runs before the unscoped loop, drops released roots, so the others keep their place.\n- **`PortalRangeStore.HasTargetBelow`** replaces `FiberElementCleaner.HoldsAPortalTarget`. It walks the removed element's subtree against the per-target range count, and returns early when no range exists, rather than reading every range for each element.\n- **`PortalRangeStore.HasRangeOn`** answers `ReleaseBridgeIfLastPortalOn` from the count kept per target.\n- **`ComponentRegistry`** keeps each Portal's inline fibers in a linked list. A fiber holds its own node, so leaving the list takes no search.\n- **`PortalsUnder`** replaces the per-hide `PortalsByAncestor` index. A Suspense hide or reveal finds the Portals under the elements it holds by walking those elements. The candidates come out in the order their ranges were first recorded. `HeldFibers` takes the placeholders that walk met, instead of reading every Portal.\n- **`LeafScopeKeyHolderTests`** pins `ReconcileKeying` as the only caller of `FiberKeying.LeafScope`. Every NUL-joined key therefore goes through `ChildKey`, whose hash reads every character since #1719. No other string-keyed collection holds such a key; the census is in #1718.\n- **`PortalUnmountScalingBenchmarks`** times unmounting at 250 and at 1,000 for three cases: sibling Portals, one Portal with inline children, and a control with no Portals. It runs under the `benchmarks` label and asserts no number.\n\n## Evidence\n\nEach new case either reads the structure the change introduced or counts what used to move:\n- `DefaultFamilyHeldRootsTests`: no other entry changes place when a root is released.\n- `PortalOwnedFiberIndexTests`: each indexed fiber holds a node.\n- `PortalRangeStoreTests`: `HasTargetBelow`, `HasRangeOn` and the recorded order.\n\nOn #1719 these cases either read a value the base cannot produce or do not compile.\n\n## Not covered\n\nBoth remaining scans need range starts held relative to an offset, or resolved through the row model, across their callers:\n- `PortalSlotTracker.ShiftRangesBehind` reads every range per removed Portal.\n- `ShiftTenantsAfterPortalRange` reads every inline fiber on the target.\n\nThe timing at 250 against 1,000 is not taken yet.\n\nNo `Documentation~` change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
