          "distinct": true,
          "id": "67b943eeda54eb3d2b413bbb6cb918e45c0540d9",
          "message": "refactor(velvet): own the recorded writes and the pass journal per pass instead of in process-wide statics (#1729)\n\nRefs #1655. Stacked on #1727.\n\nThis is step 3 of [the plan on #1655](https://github.com/s4k10503/velvet/issues/1655#issuecomment-6910564546). The recorded op list, the pending bookkeeping and the pass journal move from process-wide statics into a pass owned by each `ReconcilerContext`. With a single context, behaviour does not change. When passes from two contexts nest, each keeps its own writes.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`ReconcilePass`** (`ctx.Pass`) holds the recorded ops, the patch list, the pending parents and containers, the created set, the `Recording`/`Applying` flags, the queue-write depth and the `FiberPassJournal`. `ChildListWrites` keeps one static pointer, `s_current`, to the innermost pass that is recording or applying.\n- **Outside a pass nothing is pending.** These read the current pass: `ParentOf`, `StagesPatch`, `IsRecording`/`IsApplying`, `FlushIfPending` and the recorder. The model readers (`CountOf`, `ChildCount`, `HierarchyCount`/`HierarchyChild`, `RowAt`) answer from the container's own `Pending`. Each pass raises that count by what it marked and lowers it by the same amount when it applies, so a nested pass never clears another pass's count.\n- **`BeginRecording(pass)` states the policy.**\n  - A pass that begins while another is recording applies the other pass's writes first, as before.\n  - When the other pass is applying, its writes are left to that apply.\n  - A re-entrant begin on the same pass keeps a depth.\n- **`EndRecording(pass)` ends only the pass it names.** A range rendered outside any pass therefore cannot end another context's pass.\n- **`RelationalTreeWatch.Watch` runs before `BeginRecording`**, so a throw there leaves no pass current.\n- **The journal is owned by the pass.** It still closes where the outer render exits; moving that close point belongs to the step that applies only on completion.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`PassOwnershipTests` and `PassOwnershipDuringApplyTests` cover these cases:\n\n- **Another pass beginning while one records.** The recording pass's writes apply first.\n- **An inner pass that ends.** The inner pass applies its own writes. The outer pass keeps recording.\n- **A pass that begins during another pass's apply.** It does not apply the applying pass's remaining writes early, and it applies its own writes when it ends.\n- **A pass that ends inside an apply over a container the apply still has pending.** The model and the live list stay in step.\n- **No pass open.** An insert is immediate.\n\nEach existing recorded-write fixture now names the pass it drives.\n\nNo CHANGELOG fragment and no `Documentation~` change: nothing a single-context application observes changes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
