          "distinct": true,
          "id": "439ad73d30df74aea26bc2cab1540c1772836992",
          "message": "refactor(velvet): journal a pass's slot, tree and boundary writes on the fiber so a dropped pass can put them back (#1731)\n\nRefs #1655. Stacked on #1729. This lands together with the step that drops a pass (step 7), which is the first production reader of the journal.\n\nThis is the first part of step 4 of [the plan on #1655](https://github.com/s4k10503/velvet/issues/1655#issuecomment-6910564546), split as [recorded there](https://github.com/s4k10503/velvet/issues/1655#issuecomment-6912190915). The pass's journal records three families of fiber state on the first write of a pass, so that a dropped pass can put them back:\n\n- **Slot bookkeeping.**\n- **The trees.**\n- **The fiber's boundary state.**\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Slots.** `MountSlotStart` and `MountSlotCount` are recorded together per fiber. `InlineTenancy.ShiftedRows` is recorded per tenancy.\n- **Trees.** `PreviousTree`, `PendingOldTree` and `OwningPortalPlaceholder` are recorded as `FiberTrees`.\n- **Boundary state.** The fiber's 14 offscreen, fallback, presence and discard fields are recorded as `FiberBoundaryState`.\n- **Where recording happens.** Each family is recorded by the setter that is its only writer, and an entry is built only on a fiber's first write of the pass. `FiberPassJournal.Rollback` writes the recorded values back, and `Close` discards them.\n- **Test-only harness.** `TestUtilities/PassDropHarness` snapshots the registered fibers before a shape's passes. After the passes it rolls the journal back and compares. It fails when the journal recorded nothing in a family the case names, or when it found no fiber to snapshot.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`PassDropFiberSideTests` covers these shapes:\n\n- own update;\n- keyed reorder;\n- a component replaced by one with more rows;\n- a time-sliced park;\n- Suspense hide and reveal;\n- a Portal mount;\n- a presence exit;\n- an error-boundary catch.\n\nEach shape rolls back to no difference in the families it names.\n\nThe cases check that the journal is complete for these families. They do not show that dropping at `FinishPass` is sound. Fibers created during a case's passes are outside the snapshot. No case moves the presence members, the Portal stamp, `MountDiscarded`, `ParkedPassSuspended`, `LayoutEffectsHidden` or `SuspendedInTransition` off the value they had.\n\n## Not covered\n\nThese move into step 7:\n\n- registered fibers;\n- the pass queues;\n- the element-keyed side tables;\n- created elements;\n- the context-level presence and Suspense state;\n- the parked keyed state.\n\nNo CHANGELOG fragment and no `Documentation~` change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
