          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f7e68ffd9511ba87900630a48507fe3fb2ba1cb0",
          "message": "fix(velvet): deliver an error thrown while a commit runs its effects to its boundary in a follow-up commit (#1732)\n\nRefs #1655. Stacked on #1731.\n\nThis is step 1 of [the commit-phase design on #1655](https://github.com/s4k10503/velvet/issues/1655#issuecomment-6912782030). An error thrown while a commit runs its effects now reaches its error boundary the way React's `captureCommitPhaseError` delivers it. The error is queued on the nearest boundary, and the boundary renders its fallback in a follow-up commit. Before this change, the fallback was reconciled inside the commit that threw.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`ComponentBoundarySearch.PropagateFrom`.** A non-render error raised while a layout, ref or passive commit runs (`ReconcilerContext.InCommitPhase`) goes to the new `CommitErrors.Capture` instead of `FiberErrorBoundary.TryCatch`. `Capture` queues the error on the boundary, schedules the boundary on the urgent lane, and has an immediate drain in progress run another round.\n- **`FiberErrorBoundary.OutputOf`.** It takes the queued errors when the boundary renders:\n  - It unmounts the shown rows so the fallback mounts fresh. A boundary rendered inside its parent's walk is the exception, because that walk already holds the old rows.\n  - It reports each capture, in order. The cleanup errors of that unmount are reported last.\n  - A capture taken while a commit is still running waits for the render after the commit.\n- **Follow-up commit.** `CommitStrandedLayoutWork` flushes the boundaries that are owed a render once no drain or reconcile is on the stack.\n- **Runaway updates.** When the update limit stops a runaway chain, every owed capture is dropped.\n- **Render-phase errors** still go through `TryCatch` and the abort flag.\n\n## Behaviour\n\nThese now reach the boundary in the commit that follows the one that threw:\n\n- errors from layout effects;\n- errors from passive effects;\n- errors from ref setups;\n- errors from cleanups that an update commit replaces.\n\nThe rest of the commit's effects still run. When two nested boundaries both capture in one commit, only the outer one renders and reports.\n\nThese are still caught at once, inside the pass that removes the component:\n\n- a cleanup that throws while a component unmounts;\n- a cleanup that throws while a Suspense hides;\n- a cleanup that throws while a removed ref detaches.\n\nThey move with the later steps of #1655.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **`CommitPhaseErrorCaptureTests`**, each with an event log:\n  - A layout effect, a ref setup or a passive effect throws, and the siblings after it in the same commit still run before the fallback.\n  - An error with no boundary above it still reaches `OnUncaughtError`.\n  - A click whose drain renders a child with a throwing passive effect shows the fallback before the click returns.\n  - A layout effect that dispatches a click after a sibling threw does not render the fallback mid-commit.\n  - The update limit leaves no capture owed.\n  - A boundary whose parent renders again in the same drain ends with only the fallback.\n- **`CaughtErrorHandlerTests`.** Its nested-boundary cases now expect React's reports.\n- **`ErrorBoundaryTests`.** A child whose effect cleanup throws when its dependencies change now runs each setup's cleanup once, two in all, as React does.\n\n`Documentation~/react-migration.md` describes the new timing in its error-boundary row.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- **A boundary rendered inside its parent's walk** reconciles its fallback against the old rows instead of mounting it fresh. The render-error route forgets the walk's old rows first, but that path needs the walk's commit state, which `OutputOf` does not hold.\n- **The follow-up commit bound** (`MaxFollowUpCommits`) and `DropStrandedWork`'s held-entry loop are no longer reached by any case. The scheduler's own limit now stops a capture loop first. No case reaches them, and no proof shows they are unreachable, so they stay.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
