          "distinct": true,
          "id": "0810644a3df29ebc15bfa20c29ae6e59d34da3d0",
          "message": "refactor(velvet): split ComponentRegistry's unregister into DisposeFiber and Hide (#1735)\n\nRefs #1655. Stacked on #1734.\n\nStep 5 of [the commit-phase design on #1655](https://github.com/s4k10503/velvet/issues/1655#issuecomment-6912782030). `ComponentRegistry.UnregisterFiber` splits into `DisposeFiber` (cleanups, Suspense and presence prune, memo-cache forget) and `Hide` (removal from the lookup indexes). Every site still calls them dispose-then-hide, the order the unregister had, so nothing changes for a user. Hiding before the fiber's own cascade has to wait until `Unmount` stops reconciling its rows during the walk.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`HiddenFiberPairingTests` reads the registry's tables after each unregister path:\n\n- **The inline dispose** takes the fiber out of the key index.\n- **Removal by wrapper** takes the wrapper out of the wrapper index.\n- **Eviction by a different identity** takes the wrapper out of the wrapper index.\n\nEach case goes red with its own `Hide` call removed.\n\nNo CHANGELOG fragment and no `Documentation~` change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-23T16:51:27+09:00",
          "tree_id": "cb4498886fbbd3b2162eb8b38d0c39d39c267095",
