          "distinct": true,
          "id": "da4f087102341b138a499e1e7d81e9cb47237c5f",
          "message": "refactor(velvet): release a deferred removal's Portals where the pass applies its writes (#1737)\n\nRefs #1655. Stacked on #1736.\n\nThis is step 6c of [the commit-phase design on #1655](https://github.com/s4k10503/velvet/issues/1655#issuecomment-6912782030). Under #1736, every removal that holds a Portal still runs in the walk. This change splits a Portal's take-down into a half the walk decides and a half the commit does, so such a removal defers like any other.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **At the decision** (`DeletionCommit.DetachPortals`):\n  - The `PortalState` entry is removed.\n  - The ranges and tenants behind it shift, through `HostCommit.ShiftBehindPortalRange`.\n  - The target is marked for restyle.\n  - The range is read from `PortalState.Stored`, not from the indexer. The indexer resolves a range through rows that are still in the model, so a second detached Portal ahead of a survivor would miss its shift.\n- **At `Queue`:** each Portal row's removal from its target is recorded right behind the Teardown op, so later rows never read a slot that the Portal's rows still fill.\n- **At the turn:** `FiberElementCleaner.CleanupPortal` takes the detached entry from the plan (`DeletionPlan.Portals`). It then releases:\n  - the bridge;\n  - the placeholder's state;\n  - the rows' cleanups and pool returns;\n  - the world-space host.\n- **Still in the walk:** a Portal whose target is the container itself, or lies inside what the removal removes.\n\n## Behaviour\n\n- A component rendered after a removed Portal in the same pass can now render ahead of the Portal's cleanups.\n- A removed world-space panel's host stays bound until the pass applies its writes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`PortalDeletionAtApplyTests` holds 11 cases. The two that are red on the base:\n\n- A deleted row holding a Portal: its cleanups run after a later row renders.\n- A deleted world-space panel: its host is still bound at that render.\n\nThe other nine are green on the base and carry declarations:\n\n- A Portal ahead of a surviving one moves the survivor's range.\n- Two Portals ahead of one survivor move its range.\n- After the pass:\n  - only the survivor holds a `PortalState` entry;\n  - only the survivor's rows are left on the target;\n  - the target keeps no bridge;\n  - a label row was reset for reuse;\n  - a hovered row holds fewer callbacks;\n  - the world-space host is no longer bound.\n- A Portal into an element inside the removal still runs its cleanups before a later row renders.\n\n`DeletionCommitStateTests`: no pooled walk keeps a Portal row after a deletion ends. The case is red on the base, where the field is missing.\n\nThe CHANGELOG fragment `refactor-commit-deletion-at-apply.md` now states:\n\n- which removals still run in the walk;\n- that the deferred cleanups run where the pass applies its recorded writes, not \"once the render has finished walking\". A patch applied at once can bring that apply inside the walk.\n\nNo `Documentation~` change: no guide describes where a Portal's take-down runs.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- A Portal whose target is the container itself has no case.\n- `ShiftTenantsAfterPortalRange` on the deferred path is reached only by the existing `InlineSlotStartTests` Portal unmount case.\n- If `BeforeRemovals` or `FinalizeGeneralCommit` throws after the decision, the detached Portal is never released.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
