          "id": "c771859c26f698c746819345e0b127cd610b7740",
          "message": "fix(velvet): keep the family of the nearest author font under a weight class (#1801)\n\nCloses #1750.\n\nA weight, italic or width class picks a face within the font family that applies to the element. Several arrangements made it pick a face of a different family than CSS would, or write over the author's own font: a `font-<name>` ancestor won over a nearer author font, and the element's own author font was never consulted, so a `font-bold` label under an element declaring Mono, itself under `font-sans`, resolved sans Bold, and an element with `font-bold` whose own rule or inline style sets a font took the face of its parent's family.\n\n`FiberFontScope` now takes the family from the nearest declaration. The element's own author font — an inline font that is not Velvet's own write, or one its own rules set through `-unity-font-definition` or the legacy `-unity-font`, as a font asset or a font file — decides first. Otherwise the font the parent resolves to decides, so a rule, class, pseudo-state, stylesheet or inline font anywhere above is followed as the engine's own cascade resolves it. A `font-<name>` ancestor keeps its family, and a list's fallbacks, while the parent's font belongs to that family; until the panel has resolved a font Velvet wrote above the element, the named family stands.\n\n`InlineFontLedger` records what Velvet last wrote inline on an element and the author font that write replaced; `StyleFontResolver` and `DefaultFamilyRoots` record to it, a `LineBoxFont` copy reads back to its source, and the pool reset forgets the entry. A font no registered family holds is kept, with the weight or italic emulated on it, and removing the last font class gives back an inline font the class replaced instead of clearing it.\n\nEvery inheritor, named or not, is re-resolved when its parent's resolved font or its own author inline font moves, or when its own matched-rules key moves and the font its rules give it changed, so a change reaches the label within the next updates of its panel. Pending inheritors and a registry refresh both go ancestor first, so an element between a container and a label is rewritten before the label reads it; this also fixes the settle-order item of #1749. An unchanged update allocates nothing. The rule matcher runs only where a non-default sheet sits above the element: it is asked for the element's own rules, and, where the parent resolves both a definition and a legacy font, once per ancestor up to the named ancestor, an inheritor or an author's definition. It never runs on a frame where only an ancestor's inherited style animates: such a frame costs nothing per inheritor without an author sheet above it, and two font reads with one.\n\n`Documentation~/fonts.md` and the header comment of `FiberFontScope.cs` state the rule above. CHANGELOG: a fragment under `unreleased/` (`### Fixed`).\n\nTests in `FontFamilyFacesPanelTests` and `InheritedFontFamilyPanelTests` cover each arrangement: an author font on an element between the label and its named ancestor, present at mount or gained through a class, an inline write, a hover rule, a sheet attached above the named ancestor, or a descendant rule matched by a class above it; the element's own rule, inline, font-file and legacy fonts; a font no family holds; removing the class from a label whose inline font it replaced or that the author set afterwards; a family re-rendered away (`font-serif font-bold` to `font-bold`); and a label whose own rule appears through a class patch with its parent's font unchanged.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
