          "distinct": true,
          "id": "ef4e644fa0967a0b4e232e03d7a6d6b84bda782e",
          "message": "refactor(velvet): run a wave's turn ends and replaced-ref detaches where its writes apply (#1767)\n\nRefs #1600. Refs #1655. Refs #1692 (its first difference, insertion effects run twice). Stacked on #1754.\n\nReact's commit runs each fiber's mutation-phase work at that fiber's turn in one walk: an updated component's insertion-effect destroy and create and its layout cleanups run where the walk reaches it, interleaved with the teardowns of what the commit deletes, and layout setups come after all of it. Velvet ran a deletion's teardown where the pass applied it, and every update's cleanups afterwards in the layout commit, so a component updated ahead of a deletion ran its cleanups after the deleted one's. #1754 made a drain one wave with one pass whose writes apply at its end; this change records each fiber's turn end, and each replaced ref's detach, as ops in that pass, so they run in tree order with the deletions. It is step C of the commit-phase design for #1600's remaining half.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Turn ends as ops.** `ChildListWrites.RecordTurnEnd` records a fiber's turn end where it has insertion or layout work pending, and `FiberEffects.RunTurnEnd` runs it when the op applies: insertion destroys and creates, then layout destroys, at commit depth, passing over a fiber that is unmounted, being deleted or hidden, and promoting the deps of pending insertion effects where the pass journal holds the render.\n- **Replaced-ref detaches as ops.** `SyncRefCallback` records an `OpKind.RefDetach`, which `DetachReplacedRefAtItsTurn` runs at commit depth, skipping an owner being deleted.\n- **Waves that keep the layout commit's order** (`FiberWave.KeepBatchOrder`): a Portal or WorldSpace mount that ends the pass early, a render that parks, a resumed slice, an owed settle render, a render of a component row after its host's walk (the row renders by its own entry, #1753), and a mount of a component holding insertion effects that its commit places into an element the commit does not create. #1761, #1766 and #1753 track them.\n- **Failures in commit order.** From a wave's open, `CommitErrors.Capture` holds each capture with a place: an op's throw at its op's place, an insert or z-* relocation recorded behind later turns at the place its element's walk ended. `CommitErrors.TakeHeld` makes the captures in place order at the wave's end.\n- **StrictMode runs a mount's insertion effects once**, as React's `doubleInvokeEffectsOnFiber` touches layout and passive effects only.\n- **`react-migration.md`'s refCallback and `useLayoutEffect` rows** now agree on where a replaced ref detaches: after the cleanups of the components below its element, and before the new ones attach.\n\n## Behaviour that changes\n\nIn a wave that does not keep the layout commit's order, an updated component's insertion and layout cleanups, and a replaced ref's detach, run at its turn among the deletions' teardowns, as React runs them. The order in which a wave reports its errors changes too. The CHANGELOG states both once the waves #1761, #1766 and #1753 track are gone. The fragment `refactor-turn-ends-in-wave.md` states the StrictMode change.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **`TurnEndOrderTests`** (new). Each case is red on the base, or declares `GREEN_ON_BASE` with the cut that reddens it.\n- No existing expectation is re-expected.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- The residuals X1, X8 and Y12 on #1655: an updated fiber's turn end runs while a deferred deletion's rows are still attached, a container's placements land after later siblings' turn ends, and a replaced ref of an element being placed detaches before the placement.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
