          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f68d8fc7d5c7c3dff936cc5d999ee8b5727a2110",
          "message": "fix(velvet): run every root's pending passive effects before any root renders (#1771)\n\nRefs #1604. Stacked on #1767.\n\nReact keeps one pending root and flushes its passive effects before it renders or commits anything. Velvet flushed only the root being drained, so another root's pending `UseEffect`s ran after this root had rendered. This is step A of #1604's design: every entry into the reconciler first runs every root's pending passive work.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`FiberEffects`**: `ArmPassiveDrain` registers each context that has pending passive work in a process-wide list, ahead of its early returns. `FlushEveryContextsPendingPassiveWork` runs each listed context's work on its own. An exception from one root is logged, that root stands down, and the rest still runs.\n- **`FiberExecutionContext.Enter`** runs that flush first, so it never runs inside an open pass. `Release` no longer flushes the previous item's root.\n- **Doors that flushed on their own**: the flushes in `DisposeWork`, `FlushDiscreteEventWork` and `RenderRange` are removed, along with `IReconcilerBridge.FlushPendingPassiveEffectsForController`. The doors that only flushed now open an empty entry.\n- **Disposal**: React folds `root.unmount()` into one sync render.\n  - `MountedTree.Unmount` stands its root down before its entry.\n  - A `Dispose` held inside an entry stands the root down when it is held, so a flush held for that root renders nothing.\n  - A drain stops after the pass in which its root's disposal was held.\n- **StrictMode**: `ScheduleRunEffects` keeps the first staging's mount flag, so a component rendered again before its effects ran keeps the second run of its mount effects.\n- **`react-migration.md`** no longer documents the per-root deviation.\n\n## Behaviour that changes\n\nThe fragment `fix-flush-every-root-before-render.md` states each change.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `PassiveEffectFlushAtEntryTests` (new): each case is red on the base, including a disposal held behind a render of the same tree, and an effect that sets state on its own tree and then disposes it.\n- `EffectOrderTests`: a parked pass completed by an urgent drain double-invokes the mounted child's effect under StrictMode.\n- `UseEffectTests`' unmount-before-flush case is re-expected: a tree disposed before its mount's effects ran now runs them and their cleanups, as `root.unmount()` does.\n- `HeldWorkReleaseTests`: the held passive flush is driven from inside the walk that asks for it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
