          "id": "32c9f30bbfbf5ca09c6c769d915926857d5473b0",
          "message": "fix(velvet): follow an ancestor's font change in the same update through an element with no font of its own (#1803)\n\nCloses #1749. Item 4 (settle order) landed with #1801; item 3 is tracked in #1802, of which it is a consequence: under `transition-all` the engine switches an element's font halfway through the transition, and a label under that element follows one update after it switches. A font a class or stylesheet rule gives an ancestor still reaches a font-class label one update after the style pass; that is #1804.\n\nAn inline font write applies to the written element's own computed style at once, but reaches its descendants only at the next style pass. So a font-class label below an element with no font of its own read that element's stale resolved font for one update (item 1), and a container whose inline font was cleared because no family holds the new font still resolved the old one until the pass (item 2).\n\n`FiberFontScope` now reads the inherited font by walking up past ancestors that declare no font inline, set none through a rule of any stylesheet, and run no font transition, to the first declaring ancestor, whose resolved style is current. Each inheritor records both its parent's font and that ancestor's (definition and legacy alike), and the per-update poll re-resolves it when either moves; `ResolveBelow` descends through elements that only inherit after a move. So a font written inline above an element, by Velvet or an author, as a definition or a legacy `-unity-font`, reaches a font-class label in the same update through elements that declare none, including a font no registered family holds. An element in between that transitions its font is followed as it shows it. Where the rule matcher cannot be built, only inline fonts are read.\n\nAn unchanged update asks no rule matcher: each inheritor walks up past the elements that inherit (two inline reads and a transition lookup per step) and reads four resolved fonts. The matcher runs only while resolving an inheritor whose parent has a resolved font that differs from the declaring ancestor's, once per element between them up to the first that a rule gives a font.\n\n`Documentation~/fonts.md`, the header comment of `FiberFontScope.cs` and a CHANGELOG fragment (`### Fixed`) are updated.\n\nTests: a classless element between a bold element and a bold label when the container's family changes; the same when the font the container inherits changes before a style pass; an author's inline font above a classless element changing; a bold and a normal container cleared to a font no family holds; an inline legacy font set above a classless element; a theme-sheet rule giving an in-between element its font; and a classless element transitioning its font between a bold container and a bold label.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
