          "distinct": true,
          "id": "ec07b5de58857154a4d3986b1320b06cf2e644fa",
          "message": "docs(velvet): stop tying deferReconcile to the initial inline mount in three comments (#1805)\n\nCloses #1797.\n\nComments tied `deferReconcile` to the initial inline mount. Three callers pass it: `FiberRenderer.MountInline`, `SubsumeFiberIntoThisPass` (a re-render of a fiber already mounted, which the ancestor's pass commits through its parent expansion), and the Suspense retry in `NotifyAsyncResourceCompleted`.\n\n- Above `MountInline`: the sentence saying later re-renders use the fiber's own Reconciler and that the flag is honoured only on the initial mount is deleted; both halves were false.\n- Above `ReconcileIntoSlotRange` and in `ParkOldTreeIfPending` (`FiberCommitWork.cs`): the explanations of what happens to a deferred render's tree are deleted. The first named the initial mount alone; a rewrite naming who takes the tree for each caller was not true of a retry that suspends again, is caught by an error boundary, or is not retained; and \"a deferred render reconciles none of its own rows\" is false where the fiber's parked time-sliced pass drains first. The `deferReconcile` guards under each say what the code decides.\n- The double-invoke diagnostic's comment in `FiberRenderer.cs` now says a deferred render runs it too, without the mount-only narrowing or the unmeasured \"common case\".\n\nComment-only; no behaviour or documentation change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-23T16:57:24Z",
          "tree_id": "a7f3055e36135fc2afd9e2d50c8627712adccb3d",
